<title>ESTONIA: TALLINNA PANK TO CUT STAFF COSTS - REPORT.</title>
<headline>TALLINNA PANK TO CUT STAFF COSTS - REPORT.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tallinna pank will reduce its staff costs from 45.3 percent of operating costs to 38 percent, the Aripaev business newspaper said on Monday.</p>
<p>The newspaper quoted the bank's chairman, Guido Sammelselg, as saying that personnel costs were 77.2 million kroons in 1996 and were caused by competing with high salary levels at Estonia's largest bank, Hansapank.</p>
<p>Sammelselg said the bank will not increase salaries this year, the newspaper added.</p>
<p>Sammelselg also said that Tallinna pank will not increase the size of its loan portfolio, the newspaper added.</p>
<p>-- David Mardiste, Tallinn newsroom, +372 630 8400 reuters@reuters.ee</p>
